dialect protocol
protocol stdio.gif.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.gif.op
start op

# `protocol::OpBinary::encode_op`/`decode_op` (../🦀️.rs) forward straight to
# `dsl::variants_binary::encode_op`/`decode_op` — this was ALREADY real binary before this
# program touched it, NOT the F6-era `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut
# (confirmed by direct reading: `encode_op` calls `os_pack::encode_record_body`, never
# `print_op`). Layout, byte-for-byte, per that helper's own doc comment (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT`):
# a fixed `format` byte (always `1`), the matched variant's ordinal as a `varint`
# (declaration order, `NoMutation` dropped: `SetSnapshot`=0, `SetScreenSize`=1,
# `SetGlobalColorTable`=2, `SetBackgroundColorIndex`=3, `SetPixelAspectRatio`=4,
# `InsertImage`=5, `RemoveImage`=6, `MoveImage`=7, `SetImageGeometry`=8, `SetImagePixels`=9,
# `SetImageInterlace`=10 — `dsl::DslVariants::variants()`'s own emission order), then the
# variant's own field payload, `os_pack::encode_record_body(spec, record)` — itself a
# varint-prefixed STRING-SYMBOL TABLE followed by a generic, self-describing per-field-id
# TAG+value wire. This inner wire is the FRAMEWORK's own generic record-body encoding —
# shared verbatim by every `#[derive(dsl::DslRecord)]`/`DslOps`/`DslDiff` type in the whole
# repo, not anything specific to `stdio.gif`, and is genuinely NOT expressible by this
# dialect's `Array`/`Ref`/`repeat` primitives as they stand today (no dynamic per-field TAG
# dispatch keyed by a runtime field-id, no symbol-table back-reference resolution) — the same
# `txt-opbinary-record-body-wire-is-framework-generic` gap txt's own sibling protocol file
# documents (`📄txt/…/🧬️mutations/💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio`), copied verbatim per
# its own "copy the shape" instruction. Modeled honestly: `format`/`ordinal` are genuinely,
# individually byte-walked and validated; the remaining record-body bytes are one opaque tail.
framing record
field format u8
field ordinal varint
chain bytes
